From: Surface Overdrive <noreply@surface-overdrive>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu3: every picture size offered, the lightest first

Applications and browsers without wishes take the first size or the one closest to 640x480, and got the picture size
chosen in the Cameras page: with 2560x1920 on the front camera, 8 to 19 fps in Firefox 159 and Chromium 157 (getUserMedia
with no size, 2026-11-10). Every size is offered again, the lightest first (front 1280x960 at about 28 fps, rear 1536x1152
at 30), with 1280x720 last on the front camera for calls that ask for 16:9 (not on the rear: zoomed there, and Chromium
then failed to negotiate the rear camera again). Offering only the chosen size and bigger ones was for Kamoso, which
took a smaller size when one was offered; Kamoso is no longer in the image, and the image's camera app asks for the chosen
picture size itself (min_width of the profile).

---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
index f807f23..bb7f77a 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
@@ -580,9 +580,8 @@ PipelineHandlerIPU3::generateConfiguration(Camera *camera, Span<const StreamRole
 			streamFormats[pixelFormat] = { { kMinOfferedSize, maxSize } };
 
 			/*
-			 * The sizes offered: first the picture size chosen in the Cameras page ("min_width" of the live profile,
-			 * LIBCAMERA_IPU3_REAR_MIN_WIDTH for the rear), which applications such as Kamoso simply take, then the others,
-			 * among which a browser picks by its constraints (1280x960 for a call). Only sizes that show the whole picture are offered:
+			 * The sizes offered (the order is explained below), among which a browser picks by its constraints
+			 * (1280x960 for a call). Only sizes that show the whole picture are offered:
 			 * the ImgU's main output cannot scale (its GDC size is the output size), so a size the BDS cannot reach from
 			 * the sensor comes out cropped. Measured from pictures (zoom against the largest size): front 2560x1920,
 			 * 1280x960 and 1280x720 show the whole sensor, 1152x864 to 2048x1536 were zoomed 1.06-1.18x and 640x480
@@ -593,46 +592,29 @@ PipelineHandlerIPU3::generateConfiguration(Camera *camera, Span<const StreamRole
 			 */
 			{
 				const bool rear = data->cio2_.sensor()->model() == "ov8865";
-				LiveProfile profile(data->cio2_.sensor()->model());
-				unsigned int minW = 0;
-				const char *minWidth = rear ? getenv("LIBCAMERA_IPU3_REAR_MIN_WIDTH") : nullptr;
-				if (minWidth)
-					minW = strtoul(minWidth, nullptr, 10);
-				if (profile.has("min_width"))
-					minW = std::clamp(profile.number("min_width", 0), 0.0, 10000.0);
-
 				const std::vector<Size> pictures = rear
 					? std::vector<Size>{ { 1536, 1152 }, { 2048, 1536 }, { 2560, 1920 }, { 3200, 2400 } }
 					: std::vector<Size>{ { 1280, 960 }, { 2560, 1920 } };
 				/*
-				 * No 16:9 size: Kamoso picks 1280x720 when it is offered, whatever comes first, and its pictures and
-				 * videos then lost the size chosen for them. Browsers take 1280x960 for a call (4:3, like most webcams).
-				 */
-				const std::vector<Size> calls{};
-
-				/* the first picture size at least min_width wide (an older profile's 1152, 1536 or 2048 picks the next one) */
-				Size first = pictures.back();
-				for (const Size &s : pictures)
-					if (s.width >= minW) {
-						first = s;
-						break;
-					}
-
-				/*
-				 * Only that size and the bigger ones: applications without wishes (Kamoso, GStreamer) take the size closest
-				 * to 640x480, whatever comes first, so a smaller size on offer took Kamoso's pictures down to it (1.2 MP
-				 * instead of the 4.9 MP chosen, Fedora 45). The size chosen in the Cameras page is the smallest any
-				 * application gets; 1280x960 there makes calls lighter.
+				 * Every size, the lightest first: applications and browsers without wishes take the first or the one
+				 * closest to 640x480, and got the picture size chosen in the Cameras page (2560x1920 on the front camera:
+				 * 8 to 19 fps in Firefox and Chromium, 2026-11-10); now 1280x960 at about 28 fps on the front, 1536x1152 at
+				 * 30 on the rear. The camera app asks for the chosen picture size itself ("min_width" of the profile, read
+				 * by overdrive.cameraapp), and Kamoso, which took a smaller size when one was offered, is no longer in the
+				 * image. On the front camera 1280x720 comes last, for calls that ask for 16:9 (it shows the sensor's
+				 * whole width); not on the rear one, where it is zoomed 1.10x and Chromium's capture, given it, failed to
+				 * negotiate the rear camera again after its first stream ("no more input formats").
 				 */
-				std::vector<SizeRange> offered{ SizeRange(first) };
+				std::vector<SizeRange> offered;
 				for (const Size &s : pictures)
-					if (s.width > first.width && s.width <= maxSize.width)
-						offered.emplace_back(s);
-				for (const Size &s : calls)
-					if (s.width >= first.width && s.width <= maxSize.width)
+					if (s.width <= maxSize.width)
 						offered.emplace_back(s);
+				if (offered.empty())
+					offered.emplace_back(pictures.front());
+				if (!rear && maxSize.width >= 1280)
+					offered.emplace_back(Size{ 1280, 720 });
 
-				size = first;
+				size = offered.front().max;
 				streamFormats[pixelFormat] = offered;
 			}
 
